WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.119
Week 11: Food, Markets, and Restaurants. buy food order a meal handle dietary needs and problems

2
00:00:07.119 --> 00:00:13.897
Cultural lens. Markets, tipping, menus del día, regional staples, and meal etiquette.

3
00:00:13.897 --> 00:00:25.969
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:25.969 --> 00:00:37.827
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:37.827 --> 00:00:46.826
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:46.826 --> 00:01:13.809
Model language. Quisiera probar el plato del día. — I would like to try the daily special. ¿Cuánto cuesta un kilo de tomates? — How much does a kilogram of tomatoes cost? Para mí, una sopa sin carne. — For me, a soup without meat. El camarero nos trae la cuenta. — The waiter brings us the bill. Disculpe, pedí agua y no refresco. — Excuse me, I ordered water, not soda.

7
00:01:13.809 --> 00:01:23.729
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
